 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "First who receives, then the thing",
     "texto": [
      "When there are **two pronouns**, the order never changes: **who receives + the thing**. Both go together, **before the verb**.\n\n- **Me lo** das. **Te la** presto. **Nos los** manda. **Os lo** doy.\n\nBefore **lo, la, los, las**, the pronouns **le** and **les** become **se**:\n\n- Le doy el libro a Ana. → **Se lo** doy. (not «le lo»)\n- Les mando las fotos. → **Se las** mando.\n\nThis **se** can mean he, she, they or you (ustedes). If it is not clear, add **a Ana**, **a ellos**, **a usted**.\n\n**No** goes before both: **no se lo** doy."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Change the noun for the second pronoun",
     "texto": [
      "First write the sentence with nouns. Then change the thing for **lo, la, los, las** and keep the receiver in front:\n\n- Me das el libro. → **Me lo** das.\n- Te presto la llave. → **Te la** presto.\n- Le doy el libro a Ana. → **Se lo** doy.\n- Les mando las fotos. → **Se las** mando.\n- Nos enseña el piso. → **Nos lo** enseña.\n- Os doy el libro. → **Os lo** doy.\n\nOnly **le** and **les** change: they become **se**. The others stay the same."
     ],
